1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:03,530
Previously on Final Space ...

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:06,570
Gary and Avocato got their
butt cheeks in a hot fight.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:09,000
The Lord Commander is hot
on their trail. Oh, crap!

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,740
Now our heroes have joined
forces to protect Mooncake

5
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:14,480
and save Avocato's son,
Little Cato.

6
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,010
What are they going to do?
Where are they going to hide?

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,380
I have no idea.

8
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:20,780
That's why we're watching
this episode, y'all!

9
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:27,320
You have 7 minutes
of oxygen left, Gary.

10
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:31,060
Phew. Look, it's Carl.
Carl, how's life?

11
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:33,230
Carl is dead, Gary.

12
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:35,000
Classic Carl.

13
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:37,030
That bastard owes me 25 bucks.

14
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:39,340
-Man: Mayday, mayday!
-Can you clean that up, HUE?

15
00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:40,670
HUE: I can try.

16
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,540
There is quite a bit
of interference.

17
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:44,510
-Man: We need help!
-Any idea who it is?

18
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,340
HUE: No, Gary.
I'm afraid not.

19
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,080
Well, maybe I can help these --

20
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:52,750
Actually, I'll just
chill over here.

21
00:00:52,780 --> 00:01:02,060
♪♪

22
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:11,270
♪♪

23
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:20,780
♪♪

24
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:28,280
[ Beatboxing ]

25
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,950
For you!

26
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:32,290
This will help.

27
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:34,760
What is this? Who's there?

28
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:41,460
♪♪

29
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:46,100
Your father is a coward!

30
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:48,340
My father will come for me,

31
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:50,310
and he will kill you

32
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:53,510
if I don't first.

33
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:57,350
Yah! Ow.

34
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,680
Quinn, do I look
any different?

35
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,190
I should because
you're looking

36
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:06,260
at the most wanted
man in the galaxy.

37
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:08,190
Oh, look who it is.

38
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:10,030
Avocato, come say hi to Quinn.

39
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:11,090
No.

40
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:12,330
He's a bit of a grouch,

41
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,130
but his son has been kidnapped.

42
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,530
Yeah. I know.

43
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:18,000
Anyways, big development.
I have a robot arm.

44
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:20,840
Look at this!
Oh, my god! How do I...

45
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:24,010
Ahh! Ahh! Oh!

46
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:26,940
I think that's all
I have for you today.

47
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,840
Give me a call, Quinn.

48
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:31,510
Oh, I almost forgot.
In four days, I'm a free man.

49
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:32,720
What do you say when I turn...

50
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:37,050
Proximity alert.
Proximity alert.

51
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:38,850
Gary, we are taking fire

52
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:41,890
from the Lord Commander's
heavy incinerators.

53
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,170
Grab it firm.
What do we do, HUE?

54
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,240
Calculating. I am detecting

55
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:54,140
an incursion
in our proximity.

56
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:56,000
-A what?
-A temporal worm, Gary.

57
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,540
It's your only option.

58
00:02:57,570 --> 00:02:59,710
A temporal worm could send us
backwards or forwards

59
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:01,510
thousands of years
in time, Gary.

60
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,880
Are you sure that's
the only choice we have?

61
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:05,680
Feed us to it!

62
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:12,320
♪♪

63
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:17,230
[ Alarm blaring ]

64
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:20,330
Whoa!

65
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,060
Aah!

66
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:26,940
Mm, pressed hams.

67
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,540
That was wondrous!

68
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,410
How about covering up
that dick situation

69
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,040
you've got going there?
Jeez.

70
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,280
In good time.

71
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:40,080
Speaking of which,
when are we?

72
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,420
Happy?

73
00:03:41,450 --> 00:03:42,520
Gary, we have jumped

74
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:44,620
four days into the future.

75
00:03:44,650 --> 00:03:46,920
Wait. What? That means my last
four days of jail are up.

76
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:50,790
Right, HUE? Open sesame!
Unlock my bounty!

77
00:03:50,830 --> 00:03:52,930
Clause nine
of your imprisonment

78
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,700
stipulates that all
time-related disruptions

79
00:03:55,730 --> 00:03:57,900
have zero effect
on your sentence.

80
00:03:57,930 --> 00:04:00,040
What? So no chocolate
treasure coins?

81
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:02,270
Are you referring
to cookies, Gary?

82
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,410
-Yes!
-Oh, then no.

83
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:07,540
This is a load, HUE, a load!

84
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,910
Listen, Gary.
We're marked targets,

85
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:11,950
and no matter what
hole we hide in,

86
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:14,380
the Lord Commander will
find us in our hole

87
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,720
and take Mooncake
from that hole.

88
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,450
I know that's
a whole lot of holes,

89
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:20,320
but we're in a whole
lot of trouble.

90
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,990
-HUE?
-Avocato is correct.

91
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:26,130
We need to hide him
until we figure things out.

92
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,830
Look. I've heard of a place
that safeguards fugitives.

93
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:33,470
The closest one is on Yarno.
No one will find him there.

94
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:36,000
HUE, spool up the engines.

95
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,140
We're going to Yarno.

96
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:44,750
♪♪

97
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:48,820
Helper Hula, I've always
respected the Order of the 12

98
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:51,320
being the eyes
of the universe.

99
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:56,190
Where is E 35-1?

100
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:59,630
Ah! You're dying!

101
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,630
Dying? Really, genius?
I know I'm dying!

102
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:05,830
Every time
you use your light,

103
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:08,600
you quicken your own death.

104
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:12,010
That's why I need Mooncake,

105
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,510
or whatever that idiot
calls him.

106
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,950
I need him to live.
Tell me where he is.

107
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:20,680
Patience.

108
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:23,290
That wasn't very helpful.

109
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:31,230
♪♪

110
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:33,200
Ugh!

111
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:36,400
[ Coughing ]

112
00:05:38,730 --> 00:05:41,470
You will find him for me,

113
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:45,010
or next time I finish the job.

114
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:51,380
[ Soft roar of engine ]

115
00:05:57,290 --> 00:06:02,490
Gworplo! I'm Zargon Tukalishi,
and welcome to Yarn--

116
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:07,700
[ Screaming nonsense ]

117
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:09,900
Looks like they've made
some changes around here.

118
00:06:09,930 --> 00:06:11,700
You don't say, because
the Deathcropolis

119
00:06:11,730 --> 00:06:13,500
just sounded like
a lovely church picnic.

120
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:15,670
[ Whimpering ]
Don't worry, Mooncake.

121
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,170
We got this.

122
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:21,010
Moonobumps, homemade moonobumps.

123
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:24,850
Oh, sweet! They're just handing
out free candy!

124
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:28,680
Wow. Whoa.

125
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,620
Oh, oh,

126
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:34,120
he has
a Popsicle now!

127
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:36,530
Ahh!

128
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,860
[ Gasping ]

129
00:06:38,890 --> 00:06:40,260
I feel so replenished.

130
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:43,600
Oh, wow. Oh!
Just what is this?

131
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:46,470
There's a dart sticking
out of my chesticles!

132
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:49,270
Can you not take crap
from weird alien skeevoids?

133
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:53,540
Noted, "Do not take
crap from skeevoids."

134
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,210
Ugh.
Ahh!

135
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,380
Ahh!
[ Laughing ]

136
00:06:57,410 --> 00:07:00,950
♪♪

137
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,620
There's a quantum
gravitational disturbance

138
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:04,550
emanating two parsecs
from Jupiter.

139
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,890
If my math is right,
all our lives might depend --

140
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:10,330
Quinn, it's Triborn.
Don't worry. I'm at your place.

141
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:13,730
Everything is okay,
but super bad news.

142
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,400
You're not going to like it.

143
00:07:15,430 --> 00:07:17,230
In fact, I don't know
what happened to all the like.

144
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,630
Where did all the like go?

145
00:07:18,670 --> 00:07:21,240
Tell me, already!
I will tell you, already.

146
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:24,110
Superior Stone dispatched
an Imperium cruiser

147
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:25,810
yesterday to apprehend you

148
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:30,010
because you kind of broke
a lot of laws, like 47 laws.

149
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:31,350
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

150
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:32,920
Why didn't I tell you sooner?

151
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:34,420
That is the question, isn't it?

152
00:07:34,450 --> 00:07:36,020
The answer, I've been busy.

153
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,420
Are you touching my stuff?

154
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:39,090
Why would I be
touching your stuff.

155
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,790
It makes me look
so dreamy and beautiful.

156
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:42,930
I would never be touching
your beautiful stuff.

157
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:47,130
Quinn, an Imperium cruiser
is closing in on your position.

158
00:07:50,130 --> 00:07:52,030
-This is the place, Gary.
-This is the place?

159
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:53,770
This, right here, is the place?

160
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,640
I'm not going down there.

161
00:07:56,670 --> 00:07:58,940
Welcome, friends,
to the Order of 12

162
00:07:58,970 --> 00:08:00,780
Yarno chapter --
a representative

163
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:02,140
will meet you shortly.

164
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,780
How can I --
Jeez!

165
00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:06,280
...help?

166
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:08,020
You got me.
Are you a helper?

167
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,120
Oh, no.

168
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:12,120
I assist the helpers.

169
00:08:12,150 --> 00:08:14,160
[ Chuckling ]

170
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:16,190
So you're a helper-helper?

171
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,630
I will tell him
you have...

172
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:22,060
arrived.

173
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,130
Guy straight up ghosted
through that wall.

174
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,500
Live with it.
I can't.

175
00:08:25,530 --> 00:08:29,840
The guy just ghosted
through that wall, yo.

176
00:08:29,870 --> 00:08:31,640
Ahh!
How can I help?

177
00:08:31,670 --> 00:08:34,540
We love to help.
Thanks.

178
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:37,050
Well, we need to find a safe
place for my little buddy.

179
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:41,080
Sorry.
We're at capacity.

180
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:44,150
[ Whimpers ]
Oh!

181
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:47,060
But we could always
squeeze in one more.

182
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:50,830
Such a precious specimen.

183
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,230
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

184
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:55,100
C-can you say that just
a little less creepy-like?

185
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,770
Okay. I guess not.

186
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,500
Mooncake.
Chocatey?

187
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,110
No one's saying
goodbye, here. Okay?

188
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:05,540
I'll be back as soon as I can.

189
00:09:05,570 --> 00:09:09,010
It's only temporary.
I promise.

190
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,680
Chocatey pah.

191
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:14,180
[ Squeaking ]
Gary, he'll be fine.

192
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,950
He can take care of himself.

193
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:19,350
♪♪

194
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:22,060
By the way, I never got
your name, mister...

195
00:09:22,090 --> 00:09:24,190
Stevil.
Whoa!

196
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:25,590
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa. Pump the breaks.

197
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:28,030
Okay. The freaking guy has evil
in his name.

198
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:31,200
I'm not handing Mooncake over
to a guy freaking named Stevil!

199
00:09:31,230 --> 00:09:32,530
Stevil is a bit alarming.

200
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:35,440
It is a bit alarming!
We only want to help!

201
00:09:35,470 --> 00:09:36,910
Avocato, let's find
another place.

202
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:38,740
Let's go.
STOP!

203
00:09:38,770 --> 00:09:40,210
Okay.

204
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,310
This is full-blown banshee
screech, alarming!

205
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:50,090
Mooncake!
Sleep.

206
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:56,490
Alert High Helper Hula
we have been most helpful.

207
00:09:56,520 --> 00:10:04,570
♪♪

208
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:08,300
Stevil lived right up
to the evil in his name!

209
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:11,340
Look! We made it to the super
safe oblivion amusement park

210
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:13,140
of never-ending
unsafe stairs!

211
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:15,140
What fun! Thanks, Avocato.

212
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:16,580
It's a Lazarus trap.

213
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:18,610
Only master trap-makers
can make these,

214
00:10:18,650 --> 00:10:20,150
and people who
really like stairs.

215
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,950
At least we're not
sinking into, like,

216
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,620
a lake of lava or something.

217
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:29,420
Listen to me. Anything we think
of becomes reality. Okay?

218
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:32,360
Right. Okay. So we've
got to think positive.

219
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:34,360
Ooh, ooh! Cookies!

220
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,360
No!
Hey!

221
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,470
Eat me! I'm delicious!
I'm a cookie!

222
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,270
What? It's not like
I'm imagining

223
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:41,600
murderous killing confections?

224
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:45,110
I'm going to kill you.
[ Both scream ]

225
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:49,280
Everybody is super excited

226
00:10:49,310 --> 00:10:54,120
about today's sacrifices
at the Deathcropolis.

227
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:57,050
Ooh!

228
00:10:57,090 --> 00:11:00,060
But you're not being sacrificed.

229
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:03,230
The Lord Commander needs you.

230
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,630
What is he doing?

231
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:06,290
Chocatey pah!

232
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:13,300
♪♪

233
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,800
[ Cheering ]

234
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:24,750
♪♪

235
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:31,050
Quinn Airgon, we have
orders to arrest you

236
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:32,690
for aerial grand theft.

237
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,520
-Chuck?
-Yes. This is Chuck.

238
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:37,690
Now, please surrender,
and this all goes away.

239
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:40,030
Listen, jerk nuts.
No.

240
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:42,060
Did she just call me jerk nuts?

241
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:44,730
Oh. Okay, yeah. Yeah.

242
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:46,370
I think you are under arrest.

243
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:48,700
Hey! Douche canoe,
not happening.

244
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:51,710
God. You said,
"Douche canoe."

245
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:53,410
All right. Listen, Quinn.

246
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,840
No. You listen.

247
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,240
I'm trying to save
the world, here.

248
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:58,250
So you're going to turn
your vessel around

249
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,680
and forget you ever saw me.

250
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:03,590
Dude, are you crying?
No. No, I'm not crying.

251
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:07,190
It's space pollen.

252
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:09,060
[ Engines powering down ]

253
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:12,830
Ah, ah, ah!
Didn't say the magic word!

254
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:20,440
Aaah! Why am I the only one
covered in cookies?

255
00:12:20,470 --> 00:12:21,940
You have no cookies!

256
00:12:21,970 --> 00:12:23,940
Gary, de-think the cookies!

257
00:12:23,970 --> 00:12:26,310
Not sure that's possible.
I'm a very creative guy.

258
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:29,380
Like, wouldn't it be cool
if they had, like, laser eyes?

259
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:30,450
Aah! Run!

260
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:33,280
Oh, my God!
Think of something else.

261
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,950
Anything else!
-What, like tridents?

262
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:36,950
-No! No!
-Yeah! Yes!

263
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:39,550
No! Not like tridents!

264
00:12:39,590 --> 00:12:41,120
I'm thinking about
little trident-wielding

265
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:43,630
laser-shooting death cookies!

266
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:45,290
I'm thinking of nothing,
nothing, nothing.

267
00:12:45,330 --> 00:12:47,230
Oh! Whoa! Oh!
Oh, my gosh.

268
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:51,130
-I'm going to eat your eyes out.
-And pee in your sockets!

269
00:12:51,170 --> 00:12:54,140
You're never going
to leave this place.

270
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:56,600
Why is that one cookie
lone-wolfing it across the edge?

271
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:59,470
Oh! He's leaping! Whoa!
He's like an angel!

272
00:12:59,510 --> 00:13:01,910
Oh, my God --
I'm going to kill you.

273
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:03,750
It's stabbing my eyes!

274
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:06,180
Ahh!

275
00:13:06,210 --> 00:13:08,920
Ohh.

276
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:13,360
[ Roaring ]

277
00:13:13,390 --> 00:13:15,990
Chocatey pah!

278
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:17,990
[ Cheering ]

279
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:21,830
To the ones who live
for the ones who die!

280
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:25,770
♪♪

281
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:29,340
It's not fair.
I've been good.

282
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:31,270
I help people.

283
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:35,640
I've been patient,
unbelievably patient!

284
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:37,010
Oh, Lord Commander!

285
00:13:37,050 --> 00:13:39,010
I brought your medicine, sir!

286
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:41,150
I put a little biscuit
on the side,

287
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:45,020
just for you,
my special little prince.

288
00:13:45,050 --> 00:13:47,690
What is this?
Ugh! Gah!

289
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:51,960
I like the much littler
kind of biscuits.

290
00:13:51,990 --> 00:13:55,030
I have told you this, Eric.

291
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,370
I told you this!

292
00:13:57,400 --> 00:14:00,240
We have been most helpful.

293
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:03,040
We have found Mooncake.

294
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:05,710
My patience paid off.

295
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,680
[ Choking ]

296
00:14:08,710 --> 00:14:11,050
[ Blasting ]

297
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:19,050
♪♪

298
00:14:19,090 --> 00:14:20,760
The more you kill,

299
00:14:20,790 --> 00:14:25,360
the more the Twelve Titans
beyond rejoice.

300
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:30,230
Ahh!

301
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:32,430
Gary, we need to wake up.
Close your eyes.

302
00:14:32,470 --> 00:14:34,370
You want me to wake up
by closing my eyes?

303
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:37,240
That doesn't make any sense!
Nothing makes any sense in here!

304
00:14:37,270 --> 00:14:38,840
All right. Good point.

305
00:14:38,870 --> 00:14:40,710
Okay. I'm closing my eyes.

306
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,180
It's not working.

307
00:14:43,210 --> 00:14:46,080
-Hi, Gary.
-Quinn?

308
00:14:46,110 --> 00:14:48,220
It's been a long time.

309
00:14:48,250 --> 00:14:50,590
Come here. I missed you.

310
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:53,620
Is it really you?

311
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:55,260
Closer.

312
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:57,790
Gary...
Get off me!

313
00:14:57,830 --> 00:14:59,090
It's part of the trap.

314
00:14:59,130 --> 00:15:01,630
Gary, don't listen to him.

315
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:04,870
You need to trust me.
She isn't real.

316
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:07,100
Are we going home, dad?

317
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:13,610
Trust me, buddy.
We both need to wake up.

318
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,910
♪♪

319
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:19,610
I don't want to wake up.

320
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:22,280
Then you're really not
going to want this.

321
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:29,790
We're out! I saved us.

322
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:32,390
No, I saved you.
And I, you.

323
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:33,960
No, you didn't.
But I did.

324
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,130
You almost got us killed, Gary.

325
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:38,130
Then we're even.

326
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:39,330
We've got to find Mooncake!

327
00:15:39,370 --> 00:15:40,770
Gary, I told you Mooncake

328
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,900
is going to be okay.

329
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,410
He's a super weapon.
Wrong!

330
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,570
Little green ball friend
is a harmless gumball of love!

331
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:47,980
HUE, you there?
Where have you been, Gary?

332
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:50,480
It would sound too insane
to even explain.

333
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:52,150
Can you lock into
Mooncake's location?

334
00:15:52,180 --> 00:15:54,750
Ugh!
Uh, Gary?

335
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:57,150
Little buddy.

336
00:15:57,190 --> 00:16:00,590
The final sacrifice awaits.

337
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:06,790
♪♪

338
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:08,860
[ Whimpers ]

339
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:13,000
Crowd [chanting]: Kill! Kill!
Kill! Kill!

340
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:22,040
♪♪

341
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,280
Hello, Mooncake.

342
00:16:24,310 --> 00:16:27,780
I have been looking
all over for you.

343
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,720
♪♪

344
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:33,360
Don't be shy.

345
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:38,530
Come in and say hello.

346
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:41,230
Ahh!

347
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:46,000
How did I become so weak?

348
00:16:46,030 --> 00:16:49,200
-Mooncake!
-Doot, doot, doot, doot!

349
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,540
Chocatey!
Oh!

350
00:16:50,570 --> 00:16:54,010
-Gary!
-It's over, The Gary.

351
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:55,880
"Gary."
It's just "Gary."

352
00:16:55,910 --> 00:16:57,210
What is your deal, dude?

353
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:59,080
Why won't you just
leave us alone?

354
00:16:59,110 --> 00:17:01,720
You have no idea, do you?

355
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:04,220
Mooncake is the key.

356
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:07,220
That being can unlock

357
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:11,490
Final Space.

358
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:14,100
What the mother-loving crap
is Final Space?

359
00:17:14,130 --> 00:17:16,100
That's my business.

360
00:17:16,130 --> 00:17:18,670
Should we play a game, Gary?

361
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:21,900
I love games.
I always win.

362
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:29,280
♪♪

363
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:32,080
You know what I want,
and I --

364
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:34,550
Ya!

365
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:38,120
Oh, my gosh!

366
00:17:38,150 --> 00:17:40,720
[ Parts crashing ]

367
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:45,260
Sweet Grandor's glove! You are a
planet-destroying super weapon!

368
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,360
Chocatey!
Whoa! Yes!

369
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,200
That's so freaking tight!

370
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:52,070
That's not how we play the game!

371
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:53,440
How about this game?

372
00:17:53,470 --> 00:17:56,140
Ah, you missed.
Freak.

373
00:17:56,170 --> 00:17:57,940
Shoot for the locks!

374
00:17:57,970 --> 00:18:04,380
♪♪

375
00:18:04,410 --> 00:18:07,250
Gary, look out!
Ugh!

376
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,750
Ah! Ugh.

377
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:14,990
♪♪

378
00:18:15,020 --> 00:18:17,090
I'm going to save you, Gary!

379
00:18:17,130 --> 00:18:18,930
I'm saving you!

380
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,230
I'm here to save you, Gary!

381
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,330
The day is saved.

382
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:24,400
Freaking KVN!
I hate you so much!

383
00:18:24,430 --> 00:18:26,130
I truly can't wait
for the day you die!

384
00:18:26,170 --> 00:18:27,940
Oh, my gosh. No one will be sad.

385
00:18:27,970 --> 00:18:30,140
There will only be happiness!

386
00:18:30,170 --> 00:18:34,810
[ KVN laughing ]

387
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,480
Hey, Gary!

388
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:38,850
Don't even. Just don't even.

389
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,820
KVN has saved everything.

390
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:42,150
[ Beeping ]

391
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:43,320
[ Crunch ]

392
00:18:43,350 --> 00:18:48,620
♪♪

393
00:18:51,390 --> 00:18:52,930
The gravitational disturbance,
it's massive

394
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,530
and growing -- a lot...

395
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:56,930
a lot, a lot.

396
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,370
That's what I've been
trying to tell you.

397
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:01,170
Probe failure imminent.
Probe failure imminent.

398
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:05,470
We need to get out
of here right now.

399
00:19:05,510 --> 00:19:08,380
Oh, God!
Engage rear thrusters!

400
00:19:08,410 --> 00:19:10,550
Ahh! Ah!

401
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:12,880
[ Grunting ]

402
00:19:12,910 --> 00:19:15,620
I am not a douche canoe!

403
00:19:15,650 --> 00:19:17,690
Ahh!

404
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,290
♪♪

405
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,620
Ahh!

406
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:30,130
♪♪

407
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:38,240
♪♪

408
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:40,680
Mayday, mayday!
This is Quinn Airgon.

409
00:19:40,710 --> 00:19:43,250
Can someone hear me?
Help me!

410
00:19:45,710 --> 00:19:47,920
I've processed your scan
of all prisoner

411
00:19:47,950 --> 00:19:50,180
transfers out of
Tera Con Prime.

412
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:53,090
There is no match
for Little Cato.

413
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:58,560
♪♪

414
00:19:58,590 --> 00:20:03,570
♪♪

415
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,770
Mooncake?

416
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,440
What's wrong, bud?

417
00:20:07,470 --> 00:20:08,840
Mm.

418
00:20:08,870 --> 00:20:11,210
I get it.

419
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:14,440
So you shoot a murder beam
out of your face hole.

420
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:17,850
So what? I mean, it happens
to the best of us.

421
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,180
I mean, just the other day
I had a burrito,

422
00:20:20,210 --> 00:20:22,620
and you should have saw
the freaking murder beam

423
00:20:22,650 --> 00:20:23,950
that came out of my ba--

424
00:20:23,990 --> 00:20:25,450
And, you know,
it's actually pretty sweet,

425
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:27,120
if you think about it.

426
00:20:27,150 --> 00:20:29,220
I mean, I just want you to know
that that doesn't change

427
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:31,630
anything between you
and this guy.

428
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:32,930
[Gasps]
Me?

429
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:34,460
Not you!
Chocatey!

430
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,630
Him.

431
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:39,970
It doesn't make you the bad guy.

432
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,300
It really doesn't.
I mean, it makes the scum

433
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:44,140
who want to use you
as the weapon the bad guy.

434
00:20:44,170 --> 00:20:46,370
Look, you're a good guy
to the max core.

435
00:20:46,410 --> 00:20:47,640
Ohh!

436
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,380
I'm never going
to let you go again.

437
00:20:49,410 --> 00:20:52,310
I now know the only one
I can trust with you

438
00:20:52,350 --> 00:20:54,620
is my own awesomeness.

439
00:20:54,650 --> 00:20:56,820
Mm!
[ Laughs ]

440
00:20:56,850 --> 00:20:58,550
I'm starting to like these.

441
00:20:58,590 --> 00:20:59,990
Mm.

442
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:02,820
Gary, I am receiving
a mayday call.

443
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:04,830
Mayday, mayday!
This is Quinn Airgon!

444
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:07,500
Can someone hear me? Help me!

445
00:21:07,530 --> 00:21:10,600
Oh, my crap. It's Quinn.

446
00:21:10,630 --> 00:21:13,770
♪♪

447
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:16,400
[ Groaning, coughing ]

448
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:19,670
[ Grumbles ]

449
00:21:19,710 --> 00:21:29,320
♪♪
